 { The blockade is yet another subject that I investigated quite thoroughly in 'Mastering Chess Strategy'. Typically, the blockade idea consists of placing a piece in front of an enemy pawn, in order to prevent its advance and indirectly restrict its fellow pieces. Here are some examples that illustrate the role of the blockade in the endgame. }  
 *

[Event "Mastering Endgame Strategy"]
[Site "https://www.chessable.com/variation/12612242/"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
